from write_dossiers import add
add('duet',year=2022,venue='CVPR 2022',pages=[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],
problem='Discrete graph navigation from language, RGB panoramas and simulator-provided pose/neighbour connectivity; REVERIE/SOON also require final object grounding. The full graph is hidden at inference, but each observation provides navigable neighbours and coordinates. This is a materially privileged sensing/action interface compared with monocular continuous robot control (§3, p3).',
method='AUTHOR METHOD: encode panorama views/objects, average them for visited-node features, and accumulate partial views for unseen frontier nodes. A growing graph records visited and navigable locations. The 768-D text encoder feeds a coarse graph transformer and a fine local cross-modal transformer. Graph attention adds a learned scalar transform of pairwise path distance to QKᵀ/√d (Eqs3–4); this biases topology without a hard connectivity attention mask. Local neighbour logits are mapped to global actions, pooling visited-neighbour scores into a backtrack score (Eq6). A sigmoid gate combines coarse/fine logits (Eqs7–8). Visited nodes are normally masked as selected exploration destinations, yet shortest routes to frontier goals may traverse them.\n\nTRAINING: MLM, masked-region classification, single-action prediction and object grounding where available initialize the transformer. Cross-entropy behavioural cloning is supplemented by pseudo-interactive demonstrations from full training graphs (Eqs9–12), reducing exposure mismatch. The expert selects useful graph destinations; released R2R code also supports an nDTW expert and teacher-forced sequence targets. REVERIE setup uses 100k pretraining iterations, batch32, two P100s; 20k finetuning iterations, batch8, one P100 (§4.3 p6). INFERENCE: grow map, score actions, route through known graph with Floyd shortest paths, cache stop scores and choose final location. Quadratic graph attention/path-distance storage grows with explored nodes; no fixed-memory guarantee is established.',
novelty='Relative to HAMT, adds global frontier selection and explicit topological relations; relative to prior graph navigators, combines graph-aware transformer reasoning with fine local object grounding. Table1 isolates local/coarse/fused policies, Table2 graph awareness, Table3 training losses; a full leaderboard gain alone does not isolate architecture.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: R2R Table7 p8 gives DUET 72 SR/60 SPL on val-unseen and 69/59 test-unseen, versus HAMT-e2e 66/61 and65/60. Higher SR therefore does not imply more efficient successful paths. REVERIE Table6 gives val-unseen46.98 SR,33.73 SPL,32.15 RGS. Table4 p7 finds synthetic instructions help pretraining but adding them during PID finetuning does not improve this configuration. Verdict: strong explicit exploration and grounding architecture, with an acknowledged backtracking/length tradeoff. OSR–SR measures endpoint selection loss conditional on visited trajectory; it does not identify softmax competition as the unique or primary cause.',
implementation='INSPECTED CODE: global visited-node masks coexist with shortest-path backtracking. A material paper/code distinction is that the paper specifically describes final return on forced timeout, while this pinned R2R rollout applies maximum cached stop-probability return whenever an episode ends. Sampled training forces stopping at the exact ground-truth endpoint, whereas testing uses predicted stop. These are diagnosis candidates, not demonstrated bugs or demonstrated performance causes. Reproduction needs licensed MP3D assets, precomputed features and checkpoints; imports include legacy NumPy aliases, so current Python compatibility is not established.',
code=[{'path':'map_nav_src/models/vilmodel.py','locator':'forward_navigation_per_step, lines750–817','finding':'dual branches, learned fusion, masks and shared backtrack contribution'}, {'path':'map_nav_src/r2r/agent.py','locator':'lines239–285,295–303,394–402,452–478','finding':'teacher policy, shortest-path action execution, stop cache, train/test stop difference, terminal return'}, {'path':'map_nav_src/models/graph_utils.py','locator':'FloydGraph.path lines76–92','finding':'routes recursively include intermediary visited nodes'}],
bottlenecks=[{'description':'Stop scores are normalized over a changing action set and then compared across time; cached values also come from different histories. Such values need not be temporally calibrated. Test this with fixed logits/candidate perturbations and held-out final-node selection, not an OSR gap alone.','evidence':'INSPECTED CODE agent.py394–402,472–478; DEDUCTION','kind':'methodological','status':'Still unresolved in reviewed evidence','followups':['ScaleVLN','SRDF'],'confidence':'high for code, medium for practical impact'}, {'description':'Discrete routing and exact pose/neighbour access omit continuous obstacle avoidance and localization error. BEVBert/ETPNav add continuous control but inherit waypoint/sensor assumptions.','evidence':'AUTHOR TASK §3 p3; PAPER EXPERIMENT Table7','kind':'methodological','status':'Partially addressed','followups':['BEVBert','ScaleVLN R2R-CE','ETPNav'],'confidence':'high'}],
findings=[{'claim':'Visited-node masking does not prevent backtracking; final return can select a visited node.','evidence_type':'INSPECTED CODE','source':'https://github.com/cshizhe/VLN-DUET/blob/93e8b233164bc079a6db48b8a0a78d123ec8de41/map_nav_src/r2r/agent.py','locator':'295–303;469–478'}],followups=['https://github.com/wz0919/ScaleVLN','https://github.com/wz0919/VLN-SRDF','https://github.com/MarSaKi/ETPNav'])
add('scalevln',year=2023,venue='ICCV 2023',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7,8],
problem='Insufficient environment diversity and trajectory-language supervision for generalization. ScaleVLN constructs training data; DUET+ScaleVLN is a trained DUET configuration, not a new independent architecture. Uses HM3D/Gibson simulator meshes, navigability oracles, rendered RGB and an existing instruction speaker.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp3–4): sample navigable positions at minimum0.4m separation, agglomeratively cluster at1m, initially connect nearby points≤5m with degree cap5, refine connectivity/traversability, render panoramas, repair mesh artifacts using a Co-Mod GAN trained on rendered/camera pairs, enumerate shortest paths with3–5 intermediate nodes, then use EnvDrop speaker. Result4,941,710 pairs from800 HM3D plus491 Gibson scenes. Training: CLIP-B/16 features; DUET for R2R/CVDN/REVERIE and HAMT plus waypoint predictor for R2R-CE. MLM/SAP pretraining is favored over also using MRM; DAgger finetuning mixes human and selected augmented data. R2R reported20k pretraining iterations, batch256, LR5e-5, about72 GPU-hours; finetuning peak about48 GPU-hours (§4.1 p5). Inference is the original navigator; no online generator required.',
novelty='Data construction quality and a component-level study of graph quality, environment count, image restoration, instruction generator and train-stage mixing. Tables1–7 isolate these choices more usefully than the strongest leaderboard variant, which changes visual backbone and adds EnvEdit.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: Table9 p8 distinguishes base DUET+ScaleVLN test77 SR/68 SPL from starred EnvEdit+CLIP-H/14 variant80/70; original DUET69/59. Table2 p6 holds700k samples while varying scenes; unseen SPL rises64.59→65.32→66.00 for200→400→800 scenes. Table5 compares EnvDrop75? precisely SR76.59/SPL67.74 against GPT-2 SR75.82/SPL66.08. Table7 shows MLM+SAP76.59 SR/67.74 SPL versus adding MRM75.82/66.62. Verdict: compelling evidence for data/scene quality, without establishing a universal scaling law or language independence. Its suggestion to investigate stopping comes from remaining OSR–SR, not a causal stop-mechanism intervention.',
implementation='Pinned tree and source show a released REVERIE DUET training path, augmented-scene environment loader, and HM3D pretraining script. This establishes reuse of the DUET implementation family; it does not by itself demonstrate that all image repair, graph construction and R2R configurations can be reconstructed. The inspected source subset does not establish full end-to-end pipeline release. No model execution.',
code=[],bottlenecks=[{'description':'Simple synthetic speakers constrain lexical/semantic diversity; scene scaling alone does not certify correct instructions. SRDF improves generated-language diversity and navigation-consistency filtering but introduces verifier selection bias and much greater compute.','evidence':'PAPER EXPERIMENT Table5; AUTHOR limitation p6','kind':'methodological','status':'Partially addressed','followups':['SRDF','NavRAG','RoomTour3D'],'confidence':'high'}, {'description':'Best results combine data, larger visual encoder and EnvEdit; architecture-controlled comparisons must separate starred and unstarred Table9 rows.','evidence':'PAPER EXPERIMENT Table9 footnote','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Partially addressed','followups':['SRDF controlled InternViT comparison'],'confidence':'high'}],followups=['https://github.com/wz0919/VLN-SRDF','https://github.com/MrZihan/NavRAG'])
add('srdf',year=2025,venue='ICLR 2025 (PDF header)',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10,20,21],authors=['Zun Wang','Jialu Li','Yicong Hong','Songze Li','Kunchang Li','Shoubin Yu','Yi Wang','Yu Qiao','Yali Wang','Mohit Bansal','Limin Wang'],title='Bootstrapping Language-Guided Navigation Learning with Self-Refining Data Flywheel',source='https://github.com/wz0919/VLN-SRDF',
versions='The second supplied file has the exact same SHA256 as the main PDF and adds no independent evidence. Main includes appendices; Algorithm1 and extra scorer/generator experiments on pp20–21 were inspected.',
problem='Generate abundant aligned path-language supervision without new human annotation in the iterative loop. Assumes an initial human seed set, unlabeled simulator trajectories, pretrained multimodal generator and a trainable navigator. It is not training-free or free of human-created supervision.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp4–6): LoRA-finetune Mantis-8B-SigLIP with interleaved image/action trajectory prompts. Greedy captions form candidate generator-training data; top-k sampled diverse captions train DUET. Train/fine-tune navigator, rerun generated instructions, retain generator candidates satisfying SPL=1 and navigator samples with nDTW≥0.9. Regenerate failed samples rather than changing the trajectory pool; repeat3 rounds, plus fourth generator refinement. Dataset20,417,874 instructions across860 environments. InternViT-6B encodes images except CLIP-B/16 in CE; navigator45k iterations, batch1024, LR5e-5,8 A100s, then R2R6k iterations batch16 (§4.1 p7). At inference only trained navigator is used. No theorem establishes monotonic improvement or verifier correctness.',
novelty='Relative to Speaker-Follower/ScaleVLN, jointly improves generator and navigator through navigation-consistency filtering and targeted recaptioning. Unlike mere scaling, quality changes at fixed underlying trajectory pool; Table3 tracks rounds, Tables4/11 compare scorers, Table5 instruction count controls. The approach resembles a mutual verifier/generator self-training loop, not independent ground-truth validation.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: Table3 p7 under shared InternViT features reports baseline78.6 SR/69.9 SPL→round3 84.4/77.6 val-unseen. Final Table7 p9 test85 SR/78 SPL, versus human86/76: superior SPL is not superior human success. Table5 p8 compares1,3,6,12 instructions per path, showing saturation after6; Table11 p21 navigator-filtered generator SPICE25.2 versus23.9 CLIP and23.6 self-score. REVERIE/SOON results explicitly evaluate navigation, not grounding (§4.1). Verdict: strong data-quality evidence, but semantic fidelity is measured indirectly. Larger vision model, PanoGen and task-specific fine-tuning are confounders in cross-paper leaderboard comparisons.',
implementation='The pinned official Git tree exposes README.md but no executable model/training/filter code. Therefore exact filter implementation, selected checkpoints, SPL equality tolerance and released training configuration cannot be inspected. The paper algorithm is the evidence, not a reconstructed code claim.',repository_status='Official repository README-only at inspected commit',
bottlenecks=[{'description':'SPL=1 is not equivalent to exact path following: equal-length alternative routes and goal-radius stopping can satisfy it. nDTW similarity likewise does not prove language entailment. Navigator-based acceptance may preferentially retain instructions compatible with that navigator rather than counterfactually necessary wording.','evidence':'AUTHOR filter §3.2 p5; DEDUCTION from SPL definition; no benchmark failure measured','kind':'methodological','status':'Still unresolved in reviewed evidence','followups':['CAST counterfactual augmentation (lead for follow-up audit)'],'confidence':'high for metric counterexample; medium for selection-bias impact'}, {'description':'The flywheel requires repeated large generator/navigator training; study reports3 navigator rounds but no unlimited-round stability guarantee. Additional rounds can amplify verifier bias.','evidence':'AUTHOR compute §4.1; Alg1 p20; HYPOTHESIS about long-run drift','kind':'methodological','status':'Shifted into compute/verification costs','followups':['SkillNav'],'confidence':'medium'}],followups=['https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.13446','https://hlr.github.io/SkillNav/'])
